#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115072 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115243 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "853a04b2-591a-51c2-b80f-73f559355d9f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "239ee94c-c3d9-5955-8cdd-afff77ec3279" :question/math-academy-id "e-4716" :question/problem "Is \n$\\begin{aligned}E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}$ \nan elementary matrix?" :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation.\n\nThe given matrix $E$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from $I_2$ by applying the elementary row operation $R_2:= R_2+(-5) R_1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115073 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115244 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c56b3e9-cf23-5e1e-8c7d-c474059c9a9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "40cdd39f-29c3-5dad-9708-02c3e0de6acb" :question/math-academy-id "e-4718" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix \n![](images/03/03d58fbe64af980e170a695b5f511df7e14cd74cc894e802ce5d781642d58b2b.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We write down $E$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{2}{5} & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n![](images/7b/7bb507644e3602983ed613dbe3b630fbd4fe72799c5412272a072a39c736cbc5.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd12bc7b-1b5d-5af2-bcef-c9d0fda7d8fc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Product Involving the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "ed71f469-f0e9-5016-846d-cb70d59ab3ea" :question/math-academy-id "e-4719" :question/problem "Find the product $E_1 E_{2}^{-1},$ where ![](images/c2/c26c31fb0c03ed31508d71c394a0cac97706b8e98f495758ef1bc3cb7b9de37f.svg) and ![](images/27/2728c629af340140b991c75f58104833304f4dc82d6f2f04b29b6ddde363b349.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $E_1$ and $E_2$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find $E_2^{-1}.$ We write down $E_2$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n![](images/11/11f12b427f63eb036d2f19210ab85c0a5b279bfda547031e8ae867d130aafc15.svg)\n\nNow, we can find the product $E_1 E_{2}^{-1}\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/4c/4c46704dbedb6bb10fd40107493f49481923b4f1e524dc8f3f84d98aa4f66256.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115243 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "853a04b2-591a-51c2-b80f-73f559355d9f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82c68fda-0f42-5c48-9715-68ca5d6ebb8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463898} {:answer/id #uuid "ae743fce-b45e-5abc-bd86-752ba9bcbc46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae743fce-b45e-5abc-bd86-752ba9bcbc46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463899} :answer-field/id #uuid "01448568-f01a-5eb2-9776-853e263f1da6" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464883} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78b1bf75-980f-5157-a21e-c5aaa7d1d2bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463900} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2a98f4-65b2-5c86-bfcb-8b40e5c7595b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce2a98f4-65b2-5c86-bfcb-8b40e5c7595b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463901} :answer-field/id #uuid "124e1032-53d8-59c4-9767-8aa9b08c5f27" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11393e6b-38fe-5ee8-a898-8839130cc2bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463902} {:answer/id #uuid "1d89d028-e268-579c-869b-ea7d5ab042e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11393e6b-38fe-5ee8-a898-8839130cc2bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463902} :answer-field/id #uuid "2539df0a-7237-5aec-a2e8-de82405d21b5" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ec5e472-dc1d-5891-bb93-866a6d9b3914" :question/math-academy-id "q-130774" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are elementary matrices."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388160 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115244 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c56b3e9-cf23-5e1e-8c7d-c474059c9a9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ef815bd-f246-5489-a173-af59955aa440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388162} {:answer/id #uuid "a7b90574-37d3-5939-9d6d-f41a132e44c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{7} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388163} {:answer/id #uuid "e0797fd8-3780-510c-a616-159309484a73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388164} {:answer/id #uuid "dd6a68cc-a941-50cf-87a0-dbba7667c8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388165} {:answer/id #uuid "2f63056e-6d68-5d2d-a877-8755ac4c2845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0797fd8-3780-510c-a616-159309484a73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388164} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e98b29a-38f8-524d-ac20-5c631c095e5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6550d7b1-7dc0-5855-b6b5-da0256aaa98e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130798" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix \n$Q=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $Q$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[Q\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\frac{1}{7} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{Q}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{1}{7} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436526 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115244 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c56b3e9-cf23-5e1e-8c7d-c474059c9a9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b54b601-afa4-54fb-9b81-8e1a343fbbd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436484} {:answer/id #uuid "722609aa-a0d5-5e3b-9591-7ee5f0d9b3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436490} {:answer/id #uuid "74fbade3-24cf-5469-a14c-c1b53476a0da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436491} {:answer/id #uuid "a943f519-fb72-5834-9e86-9b373dc13537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436500} {:answer/id #uuid "afe75d39-2b1f-5943-9262-25e98dd52004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b54b601-afa4-54fb-9b81-8e1a343fbbd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436484} :answer-field/id #uuid "57d2ad5f-fd97-5e2d-883f-36f12c7f88c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "682600e4-1f6c-58ba-ae45-caa8f795950e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130800" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix \n$W=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{6}\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $V$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[W\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{6} & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{2}:=6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{W}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265982 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd12bc7b-1b5d-5af2-bcef-c9d0fda7d8fc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Product Involving the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0449b553-1b65-5cac-8598-b0d8a270a950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263039} {:answer/id #uuid "08cf208e-4a67-56fb-af8e-a3fd93304b09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263084} {:answer/id #uuid "79e21f99-e8cc-51c3-a318-a7ddd869b864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264057} {:answer/id #uuid "7e60b2a6-6056-5ea2-8a17-c6be4b8de34e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}19 & -4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264091} {:answer/id #uuid "9e4de5ce-9af6-520d-b7aa-ae9f2db45567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 & -7 \\\\ 8 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0449b553-1b65-5cac-8598-b0d8a270a950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263039} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcf3b9f2-af48-548d-9af3-5530034cb7ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265636}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d8b759c1-7acc-5a06-82c3-b179ddb571b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-130823" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{E}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{2}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{2}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{2}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{2}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}{E}_{2}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}21 & -4 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436530 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd12bc7b-1b5d-5af2-bcef-c9d0fda7d8fc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Product Involving the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "111040c6-f52f-5fe4-8365-864262986013" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436477} {:answer/id #uuid "2eb70ba9-1167-5fc0-a5c7-cfac02437eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436481} {:answer/id #uuid "8d99ac86-82e5-5e0a-9493-269c69c2ba02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436495} {:answer/id #uuid "bcbeb476-106e-56ab-bc8d-5ea75f68ee56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436504} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f4c4eb-37ab-559c-af8f-9eacddcde995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d99ac86-82e5-5e0a-9493-269c69c2ba02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436495} :answer-field/id #uuid "a181bc03-12d6-5f9e-af68-66c71236d0b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c2f3128b-e14c-5d17-b8ee-71ffa4c47e70" :question/math-academy-id "q-130825" :question/problem "Find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}$, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{E}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that ${E}_{1}$ and ${E}_{2}$ are both elementary matrices.\n\nFirst, we need to find ${E}_{1}^{-1}.$ We write down ${E}_{1}$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[{E}_{1}\\,|\\,I\\,] & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the product ${E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115841 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115245 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd12bc7b-1b5d-5af2-bcef-c9d0fda7d8fc" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Product Involving the Inverse of an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/ch